  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "1. How to ask about the existence of an object\n\nThe word arimasu means 'exist,' and this word can be used when you want to ask about the existence or availability of objects or merchandise. Look at the following:\n\n... ga arimasu ka?    Is there ...?\n\nThe above expression can mean 'Do you carry ...?' or 'Do you have ...?' Thus, in a pharmacy, if you want to ask whether they have aspirin, you can say:\n\nAsupirin ga arimasu ka?    Do you have aspirin?\n\nLikewise, when you want to ask if a hotel has a room available, you can say:\n\nHeya ga arimasu ka?    Do you have a room (available)?\n\nPlease note that when you are talking about people, you should use imasu, not arimasu.\n\nExample:\nKono heya ni Amerikajin ga imasu ka?    Is there an American in this room?"
    }
